title crypto — the post-quantum pivot, ML-KEM/ML-DSA on the doubled oracle
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the road ahead (1024-round itinerary, six-season double-seat, Rye-first crypto parity wave); Rye prioritized, send often as signed rounds, approve own design rounds, stop only at custody gates.
think Walked REMEMBER + the three design docs. Active track is Season G's crypto parity wave — nineteen Monocypher-source rungs GREEN, the key-hiding family (Elligator · dirty X25519 · hidden keypair) closed end to end. The prior log named the next crux: SLH-DSA (SPHINCS+) on SHAKE-256. Before building it, read the ground.
think Learned discovery: the vendored Zig toolchain ships std/crypto/ml_kem.zig (FIPS 203, Q=3329) AND std/crypto/ml_dsa.zig (FIPS 204, Q=8380417), both with deterministic-seed keygen (generateDeterministic → toBytes) — byte-exact parity oracles. Zig ships NO SLH-DSA. This library's spine is the DOUBLED oracle (FIPS KAT + independent second impl agreeing byte-for-byte); SLH-DSA would have only a single oracle, ML-KEM/ML-DSA carry the doubled one.
think Self-approved design decision: pivot the post-quantum path from SLH-DSA to ML-KEM + ML-DSA on that doubled oracle, SLH-DSA deferred to a named horizon (build when a second impl is vendored). ML-DSA is the PQ successor to Ed25519 (Kumara identity/signing); ML-KEM the PQ successor to X25519 (sealed session / Comlink). Both over Z_q[X]/(X^256+1), both accelerated by the NTT — the shared foundation the arc begins at.
obs Named the honest parity boundary: FIPS specifies STANDARD-domain arithmetic (ζ=17 for ML-KEM), Zig computes internally in MONTGOMERY domain; the two agree byte-for-byte only at the ENCODED boundary (keys/ciphertexts/signatures normalize to canonical residue before ByteEncode). So our Rye authors the spec's standard domain (clean, FIPS-faithful, auditable) and parity is taken at the byte boundary, never on an internal coefficient. The first ring rung proves itself by self-consistency (NTT round-trip + negacyclic-convolution identity), exactly where Elligator's round-trip identity stood when Zig shipped no Elligator.
obs Laid the rung ladder (each its own GREEN send): mlkem_ring (base ring · NTT, this arc's first rung, self-consistency oracle) → mlkem_encode → mlkem_sample (on GREEN shake.rye) → mlkem_keygen (first DOUBLED-oracle rung, vs Zig + NIST KAT) → encaps/decaps → the ML-DSA ladder. All gate-free and local; a real PQ identity key stays the custody gate.
file active-designing/20260816-161537_post-quantum-mlkem-mldsa-pivot.md the pivot decision, doubled-oracle reasoning, honest parity boundary, and the rung ladder — this round's sendable increment
recommend keep-going the decision is seated on a verified fact; the next agent-doable rung Lindy-first is mlkem_ring.rye — the base ring mod q=3329 with the NTT, proven GREEN by the NTT round-trip and negacyclic-convolution self-consistency, still gate-free and Rye-first.
